<span class="tag">Cost Calculator</span>
<h1 class="title">Florida Gulf Coast Vacation Cost Calculator</h1>
<p class="intro">See what a Gulf Coast beach trip really costs before you book. Compare Bradenton, Sarasota, and Anna Maria Island side by side, with lodging, meals, activities, transportation, pool heat, and booking fees broken out clearly.</p>

<section class="calculator-shell" aria-labelledby="calculator-title">
  <form class="panel" id="calculator" aria-labelledby="calculator-title">
    <h2 id="calculator-title">Trip Inputs</h2>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="area">Home base</label>
      <select id="area" name="area">
        <option value="bradenton">Bradenton</option>
        <option value="sarasota">Sarasota</option>
        <option value="ami">Anna Maria Island</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="style">Trip style</label>
      <select id="style" name="style">
        <option value="budget">Budget: cook most meals</option>
        <option value="mid">Mid-range: dinners + activities</option>
        <option value="comfortable">Comfortable: premium activities</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="nights">Nights</label>
      <div class="range-row">
        <input id="nights" name="nights" type="range" min="3" max="14" value="5">
        <input id="nightsNumber" type="number" min="3" max="14" value="5" aria-label="Number of nights">
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="guests">Guests</label>
      <div class="range-row">
        <input id="guests" name="guests" type="range" min="2" max="16" value="6">
        <input id="guestsNumber" type="number" min="2" max="16" value="6" aria-label="Number of guests">
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label>Optional exposure</label>
      <div class="toggle-row">
        <label><input id="poolHeat" type="checkbox"> Pool heat</label>
        <label><input id="marketplaceFee" type="checkbox" checked> OTA fee view</label>
      </div>
    </div>
  </form>

  <section class="panel" aria-live="polite" aria-labelledby="estimate-title">
    <div class="result-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow" id="estimate-title">Planning Estimate</div>
      <div class="total" id="totalEstimate">$2,150</div>
      <div class="sub" id="totalSub">5 nights for 6 guests in Bradenton</div>
    </div>
    <div class="breakdown">
      <div class="breakdown-card"><span>Lodging</span><strong id="lodgingCost">$1,240</strong></div>
      <div class="breakdown-card"><span>Food</span><strong id="foodCost">$530</strong></div>
      <div class="breakdown-card"><span>Activities</span><strong id="activityCost">$100</strong></div>
      <div class="breakdown-card"><span>Transport + extras</span><strong id="transportCost">$280</strong></div>
    </div>
    <div class="fee-note" id="feeNote">If this lodging is booked through a marketplace, guest service fees can add roughly $155-$186 on top of the listed lodging amount. Direct booking may avoid that guest-fee layer when available.</div>
  </section>
</section>

<section class="proof-grid" aria-label="Accepted proof assets">
  <div class="proof-card"><strong>$248</strong><span>Bradenton average nightly lodging used in the cost index.</span></div>
  <div class="proof-card"><strong>$340</strong><span>Sarasota average nightly lodging used in the cost index.</span></div>
  <div class="proof-card"><strong>$783</strong><span>Anna Maria Island average nightly lodging used in the cost index.</span></div>
</section>

<section class="formula">
  <h2>Formula Boundaries</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Lodging:</strong> selected area nightly average multiplied by nights.</li>
    <li><strong>Food and activities:</strong> scaled from the published family-of-6, 5-night budget profiles.</li>
    <li><strong>Transportation and extras:</strong> scaled from the same profiles, with pool heat added at $40 per night when selected.</li>
    <li><strong>Marketplace-fee view:</strong> shows a 10-15% guest-service-fee range against lodging only. It is fee exposure, not a required charge.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<div class="table-wrapper">
  <table class="data-table">
    <caption>Accepted 5-night family-of-6 profiles from the Seascape 2026 Gulf Coast cost index</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Profile</th><th>Lodging base</th><th>Food</th><th>Activities</th><th>Transport + extras</th><th>Total</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Budget</td><td>$1,240 Bradenton</td><td>$530</td><td>$100</td><td>$280</td><td><strong>$2,150</strong></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mid-range</td><td>$1,700 Sarasota</td><td>$825</td><td>$275</td><td>$515</td><td><strong>$3,315</strong></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Comfortable</td><td>$3,915 AMI</td><td>$1,250</td><td>$750</td><td>$915</td><td><strong>$6,830</strong></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="source-note">
  <strong>Proof boundary:</strong> This calculator is a planning tool, not a quote. Lodging figures use the accepted area averages from the Seascape cost index and chart pack. Dining, grocery, activity, transportation, pool heat, and marketplace-fee ranges come from the March 2026 local price checks and published source notes. Actual rates, fees, cleaning charges, taxes, restaurant prices, flight timing, and property availability can change.
</div>

